---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import PhotoBand from "../components/PhotoBand.astro";
import { profile } from "../data/profile.js";
import { photos } from "../data/photos.js";

const band = photos.filter((p) =>
  ["Canal at dusk", "Moon over the stairs", "Split pomegranates"].includes(p.title)
);

const period = (item: { start: string; end: string | null }) =>
  item.end === null
    ? `Since ${item.start}`
    : item.end === item.start
      ? item.start
      : `${item.start} – ${item.end}`;
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  description="Data science and physical engineering undergraduate at UPC, on the CFIS program."
>
  <header class="u-page page-head">
    <p class="u-label">About</p>
    <h1 class="page-head__title">{profile.name}</h1>
  </header>

  <section class="u-page bio u-cols">
    <p class="u-label">Briefly</p>
    <div class="u-prose">
      <p>
        I'm taking two degrees at once at the Universitat Politècnica de
        Catalunya (Data Science &amp; Engineering, and Physical Engineering)
        through CFIS, a program that exists to let a small number of students
        do exactly that, and that runs its own entrance exam in math and
        physics to decide who. I'm heading into my fourth year, with an
        8.75/10 average across both.
      </p>
      <p>
        The two halves feed each other more than the timetable suggests, and
        the work I'm doing now is the clearest case of it. You can't train
        anything to operate a microscope until you can simulate what the
        microscope sees, and that means solving for electromagnetic fields
        propagating through a specimen and through a lens. The physics builds
        the simulator; the machine learning is what you put on top of it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Most of what I do has that shape. The Formula 1 wing needed CFD for
        ground truth and a surrogate model to make the search affordable. The
        vortex network needed Navier-Stokes in the loss function to behave at
        all. Neither half is decoration for the other, and that intersection,
        rather than either field on its own, is the thing I'm good
        at.
      </p>
      <p>
        Outside of coursework I write for <a
          class="u-link"
          href={profile.links.tds}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">Towards Data Science</a
        >, mostly long explanations of things I had to understand properly
        before I could use them. I've also taught robotics to school students
        (Arduino, micro:bit, 3D printing), and I still help out at Linux and
        3D-printing workshops. Teaching something is the fastest way to find
        out whether you understand it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Away from all of that I fence, and I take a camera most places I go. I
        speak Catalan, Spanish and English, and I've just started on Arabic.
      </p>
      <p>
        Where this goes next is still open: industry, a PhD, or the kind
        of industrial PhD that's both. Right now: {profile.now.text}
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <PhotoBand photos={band} height="clamp(11rem, 20vw, 18rem)" />

  <section class="u-page section u-cols" aria-labelledby="experience">
    <h2 id="experience" class="u-label section__label">Experience</h2>
    <ol class="timeline">
      {
        profile.timeline.map((item) => (
          <li class="timeline__item">
            <p class="u-label timeline__when">{period(item)}</p>
            <div>
              <h3 class="timeline__title">{item.title}</h3>
              <p class="timeline__detail">{item.detail}</p>
            </div>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="u-page section u-cols" aria-labelledby="skills">
    <h2 id="skills" class="u-label section__label">Skills</h2>
    <dl class="skills">
      {
        profile.skills.map((group) => (
          <div class="skills__row">
            <dt class="skills__group">{group.group}</dt>
            <dd class="skills__items">
              <ul>
                {group.items.map((item) => (
                  <li>{item}</li>
                ))}
              </ul>
            </dd>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="u-page section u-cols" aria-labelledby="awards">
    <h2 id="awards" class="u-label section__label">Selected awards</h2>
    <ul class="awards">
      {
        profile.awards.map((award) => (
          <li class="awards__item">
            <span class="u-label awards__when">{award.when}</span>
            <span>{award.what}</span>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="u-page section u-cols" aria-labelledby="contact">
    <h2 id="contact" class="u-label section__label">Contact</h2>
    <div>
      <p class="u-prose">
        Email is the surest way to reach me. I'm still partway through my
        bachelor's, so I can't offer a fixed start date, but I'd rather hear
        about something interesting early than not at all. The CV below has
        the full detail.
      </p>
      <ul class="contact">
        <li><a class="u-link" href={`mailto:${profile.links.email}`}>{profile.links.email}</a></li>
        <li><a class="u-link" href={profile.links.github} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">github.com/Feal-ca</a></li>
        <li><a class="u-link" href={profile.links.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn</a></li>
        <li>
          <a class="u-link" href={profile.links.cv}>Curriculum vitae (PDF)</a>, or
          the <a class="u-link" href={profile.links.cvDark}>dark version</a> if
          you're reading on a screen
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .page-head {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .page-head__title {
    font-size: var(--step-4);
    margin-top: var(--space-xs);
  }

  .section {
    margin-top: var(--space-2xl);
    padding-top: var(--space-l);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .section__label {
    font-size: var(--step--2);
  }

  .bio {
    margin-top: var(--space-l);
  }

  /* --- Timeline ----------------------------------------------------------- */
  .timeline {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .timeline__item {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 8rem) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-s) var(--space-m);
    padding-block: var(--space-m);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .timeline__item:first-child {
    padding-top: 0;
  }

  .timeline__when {
    padding-top: 0.25em;
    white-space: nowrap;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .timeline__title {
    font-size: var(--step-0);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  .timeline__detail {
    margin-top: var(--space-2xs);
    color: var(--ink-2);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    max-width: 56ch;
  }

  @media (max-width: 40rem) {
    .timeline__item {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: var(--space-2xs);
    }

    .timeline__when {
      padding-top: 0;
    }
  }

  /* --- Skills ------------------------------------------------------------- */
  .skills {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .skills__row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 8rem) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-s) var(--space-m);
    padding-block: var(--space-s);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .skills__row:first-child {
    padding-top: 0;
  }

  .skills__group {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--step--2);
    letter-spacing: 0.09em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-3);
    padding-top: 0.3em;
  }

  .skills__items {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .skills__items ul {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.35rem 0.45rem;
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .skills__items li {
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--ink-2);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 2px;
    padding: 0.1rem 0.5rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 40rem) {
    .skills__row {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: var(--space-xs);
    }

    .skills__group {
      padding-top: 0;
    }
  }

  /* --- Awards, contact ---------------------------------------------------- */
  .awards {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .awards__item {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-xs) var(--space-m);
    padding-block: var(--space-xs);
    color: var(--ink-2);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .awards__when {
    min-width: 3.5rem;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .contact {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin-top: var(--space-m);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    font-size: var(--step--1);
  }
</style>
